From: DE25-Nano Port <de25-nano@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Disable unsupported DE25 HPS frame buffer

The current DE25 shell sends native core video directly to HDMI. It does not
implement MiSTer's optional HPS frame-buffer command or DDR aperture, and its
512 MiB LPDDR cannot back the original frame-buffer address.

Leave the optional frame buffer disabled on DE25 and ignore menu-background
requests that require it. Core video and the hardware OSD remain available.

diff --git a/video.cpp b/video.cpp
--- a/video.cpp
+++ b/video.cpp
@@ -2389,6 +2389,13 @@ static int store_custom_video_mode(char* vcfg, vmode_custom_t *v)
 
 static void fb_init()
 {
+#ifdef MISTER_DE25
+	// The current DE25 shell sends core video directly to HDMI and does not
+	// implement MiSTer's HPS frame-buffer command or its DDR aperture. Keep the
+	// optional HPS frame buffer disabled until that hardware path is available.
+	printf("DE25: HPS frame buffer is unavailable in this shell.\n");
+	return;
+#else
 	if (!fb_base)
 	{
 		fb_base = (volatile uint32_t*)shmem_map(FB_ADDR, FB_SIZE * 4 * 3);
@@ -2398,6 +2406,7 @@ static void fb_init()
 		}
 	}
 	spi_uio_cmd16(UIO_SET_FBUF, 0);
+#endif
 }
 
 // Structure to hold DAC configuration
@@ -3835,6 +3842,11 @@ void video_menu_bg(int n, int idle)
 	static Imlib_Image bg1 = 0, bg2 = 0;
 	static Imlib_Image curtain = 0;
 
+#ifdef MISTER_DE25
+	// video_menu_bg() writes directly into the optional HPS frame buffer.
+	if (!fb_base) return;
+#endif
+
 	static int cached_idle = 0;
 	bg_has_picture = 0;
 
